>
  <p><strong>There's no official way to play GTA 6 early.</strong> Rockstar says it releases at midnight local time on November 19, 2026 in all regions, with no early access tier for either edition. The so-called New Zealand trick is a workaround that takes advantage of New Zealand reaching midnight first. It's <strong>untested on GTA 6</strong> until launch night, and on PS5 it means buying the game twice.</p>

  <h2>Why New Zealand?</h2>
  <p>With a local-midnight launch, the first places to reach November 19 get the game first. New Zealand is at the front of the line:</p>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Region</th><th>Midnight Nov 19 arrives</th><th>Versus New Zealand</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{lead.map(([r, u, g]) => <tr><td>{r}</td><td>{u}</td><td>{g}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Exact unlock times for the rest of the US are still unclear. See <a href="/gta-6/release-date/">unlock times by region</a>.</p>

  <h2>Xbox: what guides describe</h2>
  <p>Guides say Xbox owners can change the console's location to New Zealand under Settings → System → Language &amp; location, then restart. No second account or second copy is reported to be needed. Because Xbox has already handled preloading on a single global schedule, this is the simpler of the two methods.</p>
  <div class="callout"><p><strong>Before you try it:</strong> changing your console's location can change the store and content you see. Preload first, keep your location as it is until launch night, and change it back afterwards. If it doesn't unlock, you've lost nothing but a restart.</p></div>

  <h2>PS5: why it's a bad deal</h2>
  <p>A PSN account's region is fixed when it's created, so the PS5 method means:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Creating a <strong>new New Zealand account</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Buying GTA 6 again</strong> through the New Zealand store, which needs a payment method that store accepts. A copy on your main account won't carry over.</li>
    <li>Your saves and trophies from those early hours sit on the <strong>New Zealand account</strong>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>That's $80 or more to play a few hours sooner, while possibly breaking PlayStation's terms if you register with false details. <strong>We'd skip it.</strong></p>

  <h2>What actually gets you playing fastest</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="/gta-6/preload/">Preload it</a> so the full download is done before launch night.</li>
    <li>Leave the console on or in Rest Mode or Sleep on launch night, so any patch installs automatically.</li>
    <li>Check the countdown on the game's page on your own console in the days before launch.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Avoid spoilers</h2>
  <p>New Zealand and Australian players will be streaming story beats hours before most of the world. If you want to go in clean, mute "GTA 6" keywords on social media and stay away from livestreams on launch night.</p>
